Etervale fork, monogame/issues/010: SDL2's ALSA backend writes the default device's name through a NULL pointer.
SDL_GetDefaultAudioInfo documents `name` as optional ("can be NULL"); the PulseAudio and PipeWire backends check it,
ALSA_GetDefaultAudioInfo does not. FAudio (FAudio_platform_sdl2.c, FAudio_PlatformGetDeviceDetails) passes NULL when
it creates the mastering voice, so the first sound on the ALSA backend segfaults. Also frees the card name, which
snd_card_get_name allocates for the caller. Applied by build.sh to the pinned SDL2 (externals.txt).
--- a/src/audio/alsa/SDL_alsa_audio.c
+++ b/src/audio/alsa/SDL_alsa_audio.c
@@ -510,10 +510,15 @@
     card_index = ALSA_snd_pcm_info_get_card(pcm_info);
     dev_name = ALSA_snd_pcm_info_get_name(pcm_info);

+    /* Etervale fork (monogame/issues/010): `name` may be NULL (SDL_GetDefaultAudioInfo's contract; FAudio passes NULL),
+       and the card name from snd_card_get_name is the caller's to free. */
     if (card_index >= 0 && ALSA_snd_card_get_name(card_index, &card_name) >= 0) {
-        SDL_snprintf(final_name, sizeof(final_name), "%s, %s", card_name, dev_name);
-        *name = SDL_strdup(final_name);
-    } else {
+        if (name) {
+            SDL_snprintf(final_name, sizeof(final_name), "%s, %s", card_name, dev_name);
+            *name = SDL_strdup(final_name);
+        }
+        free(card_name);
+    } else if (name) {
         *name = SDL_strdup(dev_name ? dev_name : "Unknown ALSA Device");
     }
 
